WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:05.210
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and my Season
4 countdown continues.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:08.800
For this video I thought it would be fun to
talk about the History of Dragons in the World.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.940
A lot of their history gets tied up with the
Targaryens at some point, but as much as possible

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.630
let’s just try and stick to flame and scale
for this video.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.849
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m just doing fun bonus videos counting

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:22.080
down to the Season 4 Premiere.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.869
Be sure to subscribe to get everything and
if there’s a video I haven’t done yet,

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:28.349
please leave your suggestions in the comments.

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:32.930
So at the start of Book 1 and season 1 dragons
had been believed extinct for over 150 years,

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:38.480
the last living dragon died during the reign
of Aegon the Third, nicknamed Dragonbane.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.809
At the point in where we are currently in
the chronology of ice and fire, there are

00:00:41.809 --> 00:00:44.300
several historical texts about dragonlore.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.070
So if someone in the series, like Samwell,
wanted to learn more, he’d either have to

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.410
learn from someone else like old Aemon at
the Night’s watch or from one of the rare

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.949
existing texts.

00:00:53.949 --> 00:00:57.879
One of the things I love about Ice and Fire
is that George RR Martin includes details

00:00:57.879 --> 00:01:02.530
like this, hopefully someday someone will
actually write all these texts so we can read

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.530
them in real life.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.100
Here they are in no particular order:

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.620
Number 1 - Blood and Fire, also known as The
Death of The Dragons.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.950
It’s one of the rare texts about Dragons
in King’s Landing, it’s supposed to be

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.460
hidden somewhere underneath the Maester’s
Citadel in Oldtown.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.350
For some reason it’s covered in Blood.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.990
They’re not clear on whether that’s Dragon’s
blood or human blood.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:26.360
Number 2 - Dragons, Wryms and Wyverns: Their
Unnatural History.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.100
Written by Septon Barth.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.810
He was the hand of the king during the reign
of Jaehaerys the first.

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:37.030
The septons considered Barth to be a Sorcerer,
so later during the reign of Baelor the first,

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.350
who was also a septon.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.950
All the copies of this book were burnt.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.180
But a few pages survived to present day.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:49.300
It’s notable for claiming that dragons are
neither male nor female.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.920
They can switch gender, meaning that Daenerys’
dragons will be able to reproduce with each

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.250
other.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:59.330
Number 3 - The Dance of The Dragons a True
Telling by Grand Maester Munkun.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:03.750
It’s the fictional text of The Targaryen
civil war the Dance of The Dragons.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:07.991
In real life George RR Martin published a
pretty inclusive re-telling of The Dance of

00:02:07.991 --> 00:02:10.359
The Dragons called the Princess and The Queen.

00:02:10.359 --> 00:02:13.950
Which you can read as part of the Dangerous
Women Anthology.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.340
Number 4 - Dragonkin by Maester Thomax, which
is a book that exist at Castle Black at the

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.340
Night’s Watch.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.300
The copy belonged to Maester Aemon until he
died, when Jon Snow took it.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:30.670
If you remember in the trailer, you can see
Samwell and Jon pouring over texts in the

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.340
Night’s Watch library.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.349
Careful for spoilers on this last book.

00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:41.171
Because it includes a small detail from 
Book 5.

00:02:41.171 --> 00:02:46.129
Number 5 - The Shy Maid’s Dragonlore is
a book being planned by Tyrion.

00:02:46.129 --> 00:02:49.689
But because he needs to do more research,
he’s hoping to get another famous book,

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:53.090
“The Fires of the Freehold”, a concise
history of Old Valyria.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:03:00.799
Which is actually a good transition to the
known beginning of Dragons, or at least Dragons

00:03:00.799 --> 00:03:02.579
co-existing with humans.

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:06.660
Very little is known about the actual lineage
of the great dragons before the Targaryens

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:11.319
brought them to Westeros, but here are some
cool facts about how they were used in Valyria

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:13.819
as a source of influence and power.

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:18.871
So the Valyrians actually started out as Sheepherders
in the east and about 5000 years before current

00:03:18.871 --> 00:03:23.239
events they found dragons roosting in the
Fourteen Fires, a ring of volcanoes around

00:03:23.239 --> 00:03:24.720
the peninsula where they lived.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.760
They eventually learned to tame them and with
the use of traditional domestication and magic,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.359
used the Dragons to carve out what would become
the great Valyrian empire that existed until

00:03:34.359 --> 00:03:35.359
the Doom.

00:03:35.359 --> 00:03:38.730
Their territory basically ran along the entire
eastern continent.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.190
And they were ruled by a group of people,
not just one king and queen.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:46.499
The most powerful were called the Dragonlords.

00:03:46.499 --> 00:03:58.310
Quick side note - The magic the Valyrians
used was specifically tied to Dragons, but

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:04.669
the other kinds you can find in the world
include Elemental Control, Divination, Skinchanging,

00:04:04.669 --> 00:04:09.390
Raising The Dead, Necromancy and Glamouring.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:18.670
The cool thing is that during all this the
Targaryens were actually one of the minor

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:19.670
houses amongst the Dragonlords, which comprised
about 40 families.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.280
So they weren’t that big a deal, but they
were the only house that survived the Doom.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.240
So when they came to Westeros, they used dragons
to rule unchallenged.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.880
We do know the names of most of the Dragons
beginning with the three the Targaryens escaped

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:41.170
with starting with Aegon the first’s Balerion,
Rhaeny’s dragon Meraxes and Visenya’s

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.780
dragon Vhagar.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.650
Balerion is the most famous just because of
his size.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:50.660
You can see how Daenerys kind of mirrors Aegon
in that she brought three dragons back into

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.720
the world.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.660
Drogon being the closest analog of Balerion.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:59.080
He ended up living to about 200 years and
just died of old age unlike all the dragons

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:00.770
during the civil war.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:05.340
If you ever wondered why Harenhaal looks so
melty and ominous, it’s because Aegon used

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.840
Balerion and the other dragons to roast Harren
the Black right after he finished the castle

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.240
and moved in.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.220
He had boasted it was impregnable.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.530
But walls can’t keep Dragons out.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:21.440
Supposedly after Aegon took all the blades
from the Six conquered Kings of Westeros,

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:27.590
Balerion helped to melt the blades with dragonfire
so that they could be forged into the Iron

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.590
Throne.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:33.340
After their death the only recorded dragon
names were the six that belonged to Jaeharys

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:37.660
the first and then the many that were part
of the Dance of The Dragons.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:45.501
During that there were six Greens, 10 blacks,
two that changed from blacks to greens, two

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:49.250
neutral dragons and one that survived.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:56.140
The last living dragon existed during the
time of Aegon the third.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.259
Obviously Daenerys couldn’t have brought
dragons back if there weren’t eggs.

00:06:00.259 --> 00:06:05.330
So when people say Dragon’s died out of
the world, they’re really just talking about

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.680
living breathing dragons.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.970
Dragons lay a lot of eggs and not all of them
get hatched.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.960
If they go unhatched long enough they’ll
become petrified.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.990
The ones that Dany was given were petrified,
but the magic of Mirri Maz Duur combined with

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:23.020
Dany sacrificing her on Khal Drogo’s funeral
pyre brought them back.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.840
In the book it said that Mirri used blood
magic and her own sacrifice made it complete.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:31.400
I choose to believe that it was connected
to the same type of magic practiced by the

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.400
Valyrians.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:40.060
It’s interesting to note that in present
day Euron Greyjoy had a Dragon Egg briefly,

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:50.440
but he claims he threw it into the sea, as
it was also probably petrified.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:54.420
So if you want to learn more about Dragons
in Game of Thrones I recommend you read George

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:56.940
RR Martin’s short story, the princess and
the queen.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.650
It covers things with fascinating detail.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:05.110
Be sure to let me know who your favorite dragon
is, it doesn’t have to be one that’s alive

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.110
right now.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:10.880
As cool as Drogon is becoming, it would have
been fun to fly on Balerion.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.760
He was like as big as house.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.820
Like a fire breathing jumbo jet.

